6. # TIMETABLE GENERATION WORKFLOW

Implement the following workflow:

STEP 1: DATA PREPARATION Load courses, lecturers, student groups, rooms, availability records, academic periods, and scheduling rules.

STEP 2: VALIDATION Check that all courses have valid lecturer assignments, required durations, student groups, and suitable rooms.

STEP 3: CONFLICT ANALYSIS Identify missing data, impossible assignments, overloaded resources, and obvious conflicts before invoking the solver.

STEP 4: GENERATION Run the optimization algorithm to construct a timetable.

STEP 5: VALIDATION Independently verify that the generated timetable satisfies every hard constraint.

STEP 6: PREVIEW Display the proposed timetable before publication.

STEP 7: ADMINISTRATOR REVIEW Allow authorized administrators to inspect and make changes.

STEP 8: REVALIDATION Recheck all constraints after manual modifications.

STEP 9: PUBLICATION Allow an administrator to publish an approved timetable.

STEP 10: VERSIONING Maintain timetable versions and record when changes were made and by whom.

STEP 11: NOTIFICATIONS Notify affected lecturers and students when published timetables change.

Provide clear status messages throughout this workflow.

